ll,"_score_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gate_piotroski":null,"_gp_piotroski":null,"_score_piotroski":0.0,"_gate_spread":0.2566568284002394,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.05077032054066173,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":50.3,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.008677802974289103,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":1.5,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009560394426669705,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.45202,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Guardian Pharmacy Services, Inc., a pharmacy service company, provides a suite of technology-enabled services to help residents of long-term health care facilities (LTCFs) in the United States. The company's individualized clinical, drug dispensing, and administration capabilities are used to serve the needs of residents in lower acuity LTCFs, such as assisted living facilities, behavioral health facilities, and group homes. Its Guardian Compass includes dashboards created using data from its data warehouse to help its local pharmacies plan, track, and optimize their business operations; GuardianShield Programs for LTCFs; Order Entry QA Analyzer, which utilizes real-time rules- engine technology to examine prescriptions and detect omissions and/or errors before they become a customer service problem; and Medication Spend Analyzer to break down the monthly drug spending for each of the LTCFs. Guardian Pharmacy Services, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Fred P. Burke | CEO, President & Director | Age 75 | Compensation: $845,842 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $402K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Guardian Pharmacy Services, Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.3B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 35% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $87M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.04\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 71% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.714249104599053},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $30.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (GRDN) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Price-Driven_Insight_from_GRDN_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_112726072801_1795782481.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795782481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"ti